{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1128065-penumbral-travel","id":1128065,"title":"Penumbral Travel","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-08-12T09:03:15-07:00","id":1128065,"title":"Penumbral Travel","content":"What are the mechanics of using the Penumbra to cover ground in the real world? In Dungeons and Dragons we called it Shadow Walking btw. I seem to recall an example being made that someone could walk from Queens to Manhattan in 10 minutes by stepping sideways into the Penumbra and stepping back at the destination, which would be 60mph or so but I could be thinking of something else. For that matter, if I found a bicycle (or managed to bring one with me), would I travel proportionally faster in the real world?<br /> <br /> Can anyone enlighten me?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3814,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3814-g3taso","user":"g3taso","date":". 08-12-2017, 12:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3814-g3taso","name":"g3taso","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3814_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-12T09:45:18-07:00","id":1128075,"title":"","content":"I think Penumbral travel works the same as physical travel if you are not using Gifts. The fact that you would have to deal with Weaver and Wyrm spirits would probably also slow you down.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-12T12:58:15-07:00","id":1128132,"title":"","content":"Penumbral travel is exactly the same speed as travelling in the Realm. Only if you use Moon Bridges to travel between caerns do you travel much quicker, and technically that is not travel through the penumbra as the apex of every Moon Bridge is in the Aetherial Realm.<br /> <br /> There might also be other kinds of Gifts or caern powers that allow faster travel. In first edition Werewolf corebook, it is mentioned that the caern totem Mera, who is a water spirit, allows Garou who spend a Gnosis to jump into one body of water in Central Park (her bawn) and instantly appear in any other body of water in the park.<br /> <br /> But that is always some kind of special power, not a property of the Penumbra. If you go to one of the Near Realms though, time may happen different there then it does in the Realm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-13T07:53:16-07:00","id":1128438,"title":"","content":"I was always under the impression that Airts can sometimes be used to cut down on travel time. But that requires bargaining with spirits to lead you. <br /> <br /> In general, the Penumbra maps evenly against the Material. It's only by traveling farther (into the Umbra/away from Earth) and then back that you can cut down on time, which more depends on how far you need to travel.<br /> <br /> For Queens to Manhattan there are a number of decently quick ways to get there. Moon Bridges might be fastest. But even Sidestepping and running in Lupus would cut down on time compared to more Material world travel means.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-13T09:26:10-07:00","id":1128484,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>g3taso</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1128065-penumbral-travel#post1128065\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What are the mechanics of using the Penumbra to cover ground in the real world? In Dungeons and Dragons we called it Shadow Walking btw. I seem to recall an example being made that someone could walk from Queens to Manhattan in 10 minutes by stepping sideways into the Penumbra and stepping back at the destination, which would be 60mph or so but I could be thinking of something else. For that matter, if I found a bicycle (or managed to bring one with me), would I travel proportionally faster in the real world?<br /> <br /> Can anyone enlighten me?</div> </div> </div> </div>I always had the idea that umbral travel can be from normal matterial reveal to the complete random.<br /> <br /> Since many places and roads in the umbra tend to neverending twist depending on the power of their matterial echoes, so a national road or a city path may be exactly the same in the umbra and take you at the same place in the same amount of time, while another may provide way faster travel, or way slower one. There are occasions that a road with historical meaning may depict a way of travel related to an ancient time or even more primal ones, it could be from the medievals, the far west, or even way back in time. Other roads may twist and change depending on the energies that run rampant there, like in a place that the area around the road gets constructed, shaped and reshaped time and again, will have a constant changing effect on the means of traveling around.<br /> And of course it has to do with the shape its denizens give to it, like weaver spiders or other strange entities.<br /> <br /> A werewolf need to take notes on the area he is about to roll on, or seek path finders from local packs or caerns if any nearby.<br /> Umbra is dangerous and unpredictable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12906,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","user":"Story Letter","date":". 08-14-2017, 07:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-14T15:14:50-07:00","id":1128975,"title":"","content":"I tend to expect walking or running on the ground in the Penumbra covers roughly the same amount of distance over time as in the material realm, assuming nothing <i>interesting</i> happens, like walking your way into another umbral realm, walking into a fae trod, etc., and the farther out into the Umbral Realms you get, the more likely it is for something <i>interesting</i> to happen to time and space. I figure the same would apply to flight: a flying creature in the penumbra would travel about as fast as a flying creature in the material realm, unless something <i>interesting</i> happens.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13713-wilson","name":"Wilson","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}